The '''1997 Football League Cup final''' was played between [[Middlesbrough F.C.|Middlesbrough]] and [[Leicester City F.C.|Leicester City]]. The first game, at [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|Wembley Stadium]] on Sunday 6 April 1997, ended in a 1–1 draw after [[extra time]]. [[Fabrizio Ravanelli]] opened the scoring only for Leicester's [[Emile Heskey]] to equalise in the last minute of extra time. Heskey was fortunate to be on the field, having committed what was a bookable foul on Boro captain [[Nigel Pearson]] after already being booked. Leicester won the replay, and their second [[Football League Cup|League Cup]], in the game played at [[Hillsborough Stadium]] on 16 April 1997 with another extra-time goal, this time from [[Steve Claridge]].<ref>{{cite web |title=Coca Cola Cup 1996/97 |url=http://www.soccerbase.com/tournaments/tournament.sd?tourn_id=489 |publisher=Soccerbase |access-date=8 December 2016}}</ref>

This was the last year that the Football League Cup final was decided by a replay.<ref>{{cite web|title=The Football League Cup|url=http://www.soccer.mistral.co.uk/books/flctext.htm|website=soccer.mistral.co.uk|access-date=8 December 2016|archive-date=5 October 2018|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20181005085103/http://www.soccer.mistral.co.uk/books/flctext.htm|url-status=dead}}</ref>

